<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1994</h1><p class="ref-lede">1994 in world history: 14 events, 9 deaths and 1 state that came to an end. 190 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1990">1990</a><a href="/years/1991">1991</a><a href="/years/1992">1992</a><a href="/years/1993">1993</a><a href="/years/1994" aria-current="page">1994</a><a href="/years/1995">1995</a><a href="/years/1996">1996</a><a href="/years/1997">1997</a><a href="/years/1998">1998</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">NAFTA takes effect between the United States, Canada and Mexico</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-american-free-trade-agreement">North American Free Trade Agreement</a> came into force, phasing out most tariffs among the three countries and creating one of the world's largest free-trade areas. It was replaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-mexico-canada-agreement">USMCA</a> in 2020.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-5">5 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nirvana's Kurt Cobain dies in Seattle</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Kurt Cobain, singer and guitarist of Nirvana, died at his Seattle home aged 27; his body was found three days later. His death closed the band that had carried grunge into the mainstream.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-7">7 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Genocide against the Tutsi begins in Rwanda</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hours after President Habyarimana's aircraft was shot down, extremists began killing Tutsi and moderate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a>. In about 100 days an estimated 500,000 to 800,000 people were murdered.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">Genocide</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-27">27 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">South Africa holds its first all-race elections</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Millions of Black South Africans voted for the first time. The ANC won decisively and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a> became president, ending the apartheid order. The date is now Freedom Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-6">6 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Channel Tunnel is formally opened</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii">Elizabeth II</a> and President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-mitterrand">François Mitterrand</a> opened the 50 km rail tunnel under the Channel. It gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> its first fixed link to the Continent since the Ice Age.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-19">19 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis dies in New York</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The former First Lady died aged 64. Her composure after her husband's assassination in 1963 made her an enduring public figure, and she later worked as a book editor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-17">17 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">O. J. Simpson leads police on a televised chase</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">About 95 million viewers watched police follow a white Ford Bronco carrying the former football star along <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> freeways. Simpson was later acquitted of murdering his ex-wife and her friend.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-16">16 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fragments of Comet Shoemaker-Levy 9 begin hitting Jupiter</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Over six days some 21 fragments of the comet slammed into Jupiter, the first collision between solar system bodies ever observed. They left dark scars in the atmosphere larger than Earth.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/real-plan">Real Plan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Real Plan, or Plano Real, was the economic stabilisation programme that ended chronic hyperinflation in Brazil in 1994.</p></div></li></ol></section>
